<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
                      http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd"
    objectQuotingStrategy="QUOTE_ONLY_RESERVED_WORDS">

    <!--
      Records, at every start, what a rolled-back release left unrecorded. Server 6.5.5, the release before step C,
      writes no revisions: if
      production runs it again after step C, its uploads raise lock_version without a revision and its new
      submissions have none. On the next start of a release with the journal, this writes one explicit gap revision
      for each such submission: kind BASELINE, command GAP_REPAIR, actor MIGRATION, at the current lock_version,
      with previous_version naming the head it jumps from (NULL for a submission created in the window). The
      versions in between are recorded as unknown, never as silent.

      It skips a submission that has a revision at or above its lock_version. One whose head is above it cannot
      happen through the application; the reconciliation check reports it, and so a start never fails on it. A
      write that changed a row without raising its version (hand-written SQL) is not a gap this can record; the
      reconciliation check reports that too.

      When it looks: it reads every submission (one index probe each, see the rehearsal numbers in
      docs/agent-context/active-production-interface.md) only when one of two cheap signals says a gap may exist:
      - an outbox row without a version above journal.outbox_watermark: a release without the journal wrote since
        the last start (the newest such row is one backward probe of idx_outbox_unversioned; an EXISTS here would
        read the whole outbox when no row qualifies, about 0.1 s on 62,000 rows);
      - a changeset other than this one ran since this one last ran: this deploy applied changesets, and one might
        have raised versions (one read of databasechangelog, which Liquibase updates for every changeset it runs).
      Otherwise the statement's one-time filter is false and it reads nothing. The signals are part of the
      statement, not a Liquibase precondition: a failed precondition on a run-always changeset adds a row to
      databasechangelog at every start. Afterwards it moves the watermark to the newest outbox row. A version raised
      by SQL outside a deploy leaves neither signal: check 11b counts it, and running this INSERT by hand without
      its signals records it.

      runAlways and runOrder="last": Liquibase runs it on every update, after every other changeset of the changelog,
      wherever later ones are added. So a later changeset that raises versions without revisions (a data repair that
      broke the rule in active-production-interface.md) is recorded as a gap at the same start, instead of making
      every re-send of those submissions fail until the next start.

      Rollback: nothing to undo; the gap revisions stay with the journal. It refuses nothing either: this changeset
      runs at every start, and Liquibase records each run as the latest, so every later rollback begins here. A
      refusal here would block those, unrelated ones included; the rollbacks that remove a guard refuse instead.
    -->
    <changeSet id="20261124-c08-submission-revision-gap-repair" author="datarun" runAlways="true" runOrder="last">
        <!-- The statement's estimated cost passes jit_above_cost: without this, every start compiles it (about 40 ms)
             even when the cue lets it read nothing. -->
        <sql>SET LOCAL jit = off</sql>
        <sql>
            INSERT INTO journal.submission_revision (submission_id, version, previous_version, kind, command,
                                                     actor_system, form_data, metadata)
            SELECT s.id, s.lock_version,
                   (SELECT max(h.version) FROM journal.submission_revision h WHERE h.submission_id = s.id),
                   'BASELINE', 'GAP_REPAIR', 'MIGRATION', s.form_data, journal.submission_revision_metadata(s)
            FROM data_submission s
            WHERE (coalesce((SELECT max(o.outbox_id) FROM outbox o WHERE o.submission_version IS NULL), 0)
                       &gt; coalesce((SELECT w.outbox_id FROM journal.outbox_watermark w), 0)
                   OR coalesce((SELECT c.id FROM databasechangelog c ORDER BY c.orderexecuted DESC LIMIT 1), '')
                      &lt;&gt; '20261124-c08-submission-revision-gap-repair')
              AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM journal.submission_revision r
                              WHERE r.submission_id = s.id AND r.version >= s.lock_version)
        </sql>
        <sql>
            INSERT INTO journal.outbox_watermark (outbox_id)
            SELECT coalesce(max(outbox_id), 0) FROM outbox
            ON CONFLICT (singleton) DO UPDATE SET outbox_id = excluded.outbox_id
        </sql>
        <rollback/>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
